{
  "file_type": "did_character_template",
  "file_version": 4,
  "template": {
    "name": "Mistborn RPG",
    "description": "<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">We are playing in the world of Brandon Sanderson Mistborn, based on the rules of the offical Mistborn Advanture Game, but using this system with some changes.</p>",
    "player_instructions": "<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">In this game, metals govern all supernatural power: <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Allomancy burns, Feruchemy stores, and Hemalurgy steals</span>.</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Allomancy</span> and <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Feruchemy</span> are passed down through bloodlines and cannot be learned through study. A person born with the potential often remains dormant until experiencing extreme trauma, physical danger, or an emotional breakdown, an awakening called <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Snapping</span>.</p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- Unlike the other two, <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Hemalurgy is not hereditary</span>. It is an unnatural, artificial art gained by impaling someone through specific spiritual bind-points with a metal spike, killing them. The spike captures a piece of the victim's soul and power, and is then immediately driven into the recipient’s body to graft the stolen trait onto them.</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">Core Character Builds:</p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Full</span> <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Mistborn</span>: A rare individual who can burn all 16 Allomantic metals. Choose <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Spellcasting</span> <span style=\" font-style:italic;\">(Cost: 6 IP)</span>. (Note: Increased to 6 IP due to the immense versatility and power of 16 Allomantic abilities).</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Full Feruchemist </span>(Keeper): A rare individual who can store and tap attributes in all 16 Feruchemical metals. Choose <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Spellcasting</span><span style=\" font-style:italic;\"> (Cost: 6 IP)</span>. (Note: Increased to 6 IP due to the immense versatility and power of 16 metalminds).</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Misting</span>: A person who can burn exactly <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">one</span> of the 16 Allomantic metals. Choose <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Magic</span> <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Novice</span> <span style=\" font-style:italic;\">(Cost: 2 IP) </span>and select your Allomantic metal.</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Ferring</span>: A person who can store and tap exactly <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">one</span> of the 16 Feruchemical metals. Choose <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Magic</span> <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Novice</span><span style=\" font-style:italic;\"> (Cost: 2 IP)</span> and select your Feruchemical metal.</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Twinborn</span>: A person who possesses <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">one </span><span style=\" font-weight:700; text-decoration: underline;\">Allomantic</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\"> metal and one </span><span style=\" font-weight:700; text-decoration: underline;\">Feruchemical</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\"> metal.</span></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">Choose <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Magic</span> <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Novice</span> <span style=\" text-decoration: underline;\">twice</span> <span style=\" font-style:italic;\">(Cost: 4 IP total)</span> once for your Allomantic metal and once for your Feruchemical metal. (If you choose the same metal for both, you are a <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Compounder</span>, allowing you to burn your metalminds for supercharged bursts).</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Kandra</span>: A creature that can shapeshift by consuming the flesh of a corpse and using its bones. Every Kandra possesses sentience and supernatural traits granted by at least one Hemalurgic Blessing (two spikes). Choose<span style=\" font-weight:700;\"> Born of Soil</span> <span style=\" font-style:italic;\">(Cost: 4 IP)</span>, which is adapted as <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Kandra</span> <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Mimicry</span>.</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Hemalurgic</span> <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Spikes</span>: There is no hard limit on how many spikes you can take, but<span style=\" text-decoration: underline;\"> each spike tears your spirit and corrupts your soul</span>, permanently reducing your mental/spiritual defenses and leaving you vulnerable to the whispers and control of dark forces (like Ruin or Brass/Zinc Allomancy).</p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">- <span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Mundane</span> (Non-Magical Person): You have no supernatural abilities at character creation, leaving all your starting IP free for combat stunts, physical feats, and worldly skills. You retain the potential to Snap later in the campaign through story-driven trauma or gain a Hemalurgic spike.</p>",
    "rules": {
      "level": 1,
      "extra_ip": 0,
      "species_mode": "normal",
      "starting_hearts": null,
      "starting_at": null,
      "allow_custom_improvements": true,
      "allowed_ability_array_ids": [],
      "free_heightened_ability_slots": 2,
      "restrict_ability_dice_to_allowed_arrays": false,
      "improvement_mode": "ban",
